`o 37 r 1(1) the Act is the Choice of Court Agreements Act` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is the Choice of Court Agreements Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Act” means the Choice of Court Agreements Act"

-- src:5269 | 1. —(1) In this Order — “Act” means the Choice of Court Agreements Act, and any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act;
