    IF `the body is the General Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Court” means the General Division"

-- src:5271 | “Court order” means an order of the Court — ( a )
-- src:5272 | for a foreign judgment to be recognised, or recognised and enforced, under the Act; or
-- src:5273 | ( b )
-- src:5274 | for a judicial settlement to be enforced under the Act.
@ref O 37 r 1(1) “Court order” (src:5271-5274)
GIVEN `it is an order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for a foreign judgment to be recognised, or recognised and enforced, under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for a judicial settlement to be enforced under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 37 r 1(1) the order is a Court order` MEANS
    IF `it is an order of the Court` AND (`it is for a foreign judgment to be recognised, or recognised and enforced, under the Act` OR `it is for a judicial settlement to be enforced under the Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Court order” means an order of the Court — (a) for a foreign judgment to be recognised, or recognised and enforced, under the Act; or (b) for a judicial settlement to be enforced under the Act"

-- src:5275 | (2) Expressions used in this Order which are used in the Act have the same meanings in this Order as in the Act.
@ref O 37 r 1(2) (src:5275-5275)
GIVEN `the expression is used in this Order and is used in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 37 r 1(2) the expression has the same meaning in this Order as in the Act` MEANS
    IF `the expression is used in this Order and is used in the Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the meaning itself is the Act's, which is not among the sources
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Expressions used in this Order which are used in the Act"

DECLARE `o 37 r 1(3) who exercises a power of the Court` IS ONE OF
    `o 37 r 1(3) a Judge sitting in chambers`
    `o 37 r 1(3) the Registrar`
    `o 37 r 1(3) someone else`

-- src:5276 | (3) The powers conferred on the Court by the Act may be exercised by a Judge sitting in chambers and the Registrar.
@ref O 37 r 1(3) (src:5276-5276)
GIVEN who IS A `o 37 r 1(3) who exercises a power of the Court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 37 r 1(3) the power conferred on the Court by the Act may be exercised by` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `o 37 r 1(3) a Judge sitting in chambers` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 37 r 1(3) the Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 37 r 1(3) someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be exercised by a Judge sitting in chambers and the Registrar" names two persons and says nothing of anyone else

