      way IS A `o 34 r 2 way an application is made`
      `the application is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 37 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application without notice supported by an affidavit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is an application under section 13 for a foreign judgment to be recognised or recognised and enforced` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application under section 13 for a foreign judgment ... to be recognised, or to be recognised and enforced"
        IF way EQUALS `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice` AND `the application is supported by an affidavit` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be made by originating application without notice supported by an affidavit"; the text does not say what follows (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do)

-- Paragraph (2): "(e) either of the following: (i) ... (ii) ..." is read as satisfied by either limb, or both (a fork, NOTES.md).
-- Limbs (b), (c) and (i) are owed only "where" their condition holds.
DECLARE `o 37 r 2(2) supporting affidavit` HAS
    `o 37 r 2(2) it states the matters to the best of the information or belief of the deponent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(2)(a) it states that the judgment is a foreign judgment within the meaning of section 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(2)(b) it states that the judgment or that part has effect in the State of origin` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(2)(c) it states that the judgment or that part is enforceable in the State of origin` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(2)(d) it states that the exclusive choice of court agreement was concluded in a civil or commercial matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(2)(e)(i) it states that at the date of the application the foreign judgment, or the part, has not been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(2)(e)(ii) it states the amount in respect of which, at the date of the application, the foreign judgment, or the part, remains unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(2)(f) it states that the foreign judgment does not relate to a matter mentioned in section 9 or 10` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(2)(g) it states that there are no circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court must refuse to recognise or enforce` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(2)(h) it states whether there are any circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(2)(i) it states each reason why the Court should nevertheless recognise or enforce the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:5278 | 2. —(1) An application under section 13 for a foreign judgment, or a part of a foreign judgment, to be recognised, or to be recognised and enforced, in the same manner and to the same extent as a judgment issued by the General Division must be made by originating application without notice supported by an affidavit. (2) The supporting affidavit must state, to the best of the information or belief of the deponent — ( a )
-- src:5279 | that the judgment, the whole or part of which is to be recognised or recognised and enforced, is a foreign judgment within the meaning of section 2(1);
-- src:5280 | ( b )
-- src:5281 | where the foreign judgment or part of the foreign judgment is to be recognised, that the judgment or that part (as the case may be) has effect in the State of origin;
-- src:5282 | ( c )
-- src:5283 | where the foreign judgment or part of the foreign judgment is to be enforced, that the judgment or that part (as the case may be) is enforceable in the State of origin;
-- src:5284 | ( d )
-- src:5285 | that the exclusive choice of court agreement, applicable to the dispute in relation to which the foreign judgment was obtained, was concluded in a civil or commercial matter;
-- src:5286 | ( e )
-- src:5287 | either of the following: (i)
-- src:5288 | that at the date of the application, the foreign judgment, or the part of the foreign judgment to be recognised or recognised and enforced, has not been satisfied;
-- src:5289 | (ii)
-- src:5290 | the amount in respect of which, at the date of the application, the foreign judgment, or the part of the foreign judgment to be recognised or recognised and enforced, remains unsatisfied;
-- src:5291 | ( f )
-- src:5292 | that the foreign judgment does not relate to a matter mentioned in section 9 or 10 to which the Act does not apply;
-- src:5293 | ( g )
-- src:5294 | that there are no circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court must refuse to recognise or enforce the foreign judgment;
-- src:5295 | ( h )
-- src:5296 | whether there are any circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce the foreign judgment; and
-- src:5297 | ( i )
-- src:5298 | where there are circumstances in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce the foreign judgment, each reason why the Court should nevertheless recognise or enforce the judgment.
@ref O 37 r 2(2) (src:5278-5298)
GIVEN affidavit IS AN `o 37 r 2(2) supporting affidavit`
      `the foreign judgment or part is to be recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign judgment or part is to be enforced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are circumstances in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce the foreign judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 37 r 2(2) the supporting affidavit states what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 37 r 2(2) it states the matters to the best of the information or belief of the deponent` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) is a bare "must state, to the best of the information or belief of the deponent"; the text does not say what follows (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do)
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 37 r 2(2)(a) it states that the judgment is a foreign judgment within the meaning of section 2(1)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2)(a) is a bare "must state"; the text does not say what follows
        IF `the foreign judgment or part is to be recognised` AND (NOT affidavit's `o 37 r 2(2)(b) it states that the judgment or that part has effect in the State of origin`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2)(b) is a bare "must state"; owed only where the judgment or part is to be recognised
        IF `the foreign judgment or part is to be enforced` AND (NOT affidavit's `o 37 r 2(2)(c) it states that the judgment or that part is enforceable in the State of origin`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2)(c) is a bare "must state"; owed only where the judgment or part is to be enforced
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 37 r 2(2)(d) it states that the exclusive choice of court agreement was concluded in a civil or commercial matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2)(d) is a bare "must state"; the text does not say what follows
        IF (NOT affidavit's `o 37 r 2(2)(e)(i) it states that at the date of the application the foreign judgment, or the part, has not been satisfied`) AND (NOT affidavit's `o 37 r 2(2)(e)(ii) it states the amount in respect of which, at the date of the application, the foreign judgment, or the part, remains unsatisfied`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2)(e) is a bare "either of the following"; the text does not say what follows if neither is stated
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 37 r 2(2)(f) it states that the foreign judgment does not relate to a matter mentioned in section 9 or 10` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2)(f) is a bare "must state"; the text does not say what follows
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 37 r 2(2)(g) it states that there are no circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court must refuse to recognise or enforce` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2)(g) is a bare "must state"; the text does not say what follows
        IF NOT affidavit's `o 37 r 2(2)(h) it states whether there are any circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2)(h) is a bare "must state"; the text does not say what follows
        IF `there are circumstances in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce the foreign judgment` AND (NOT affidavit's `o 37 r 2(2)(i) it states each reason why the Court should nevertheless recognise or enforce the judgment`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2)(i) is a bare "must state"; owed only where there are circumstances in which the Court may refuse
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `o 37 r 2(3) documents exhibited to the supporting affidavit` HAS
    `o 37 r 2(3)(a) it exhibits a complete and certified copy of the foreign judgment (including the reasons, if any, for the decision)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(3)(b) it exhibits the exclusive choice of court agreement, a certified copy of it or any other evidence of its existence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(3)(c) it exhibits the original or a certified copy of a document showing that the party in default was notified of the document by which the proceedings were instituted or an equivalent document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(3)(d)(i) it exhibits any other documents necessary to establish that the foreign judgment has effect in the State of origin` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(3)(d)(ii) it exhibits any other documents necessary to establish that the judgment or that part is enforceable in the State of origin` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 2(3)(d)(iii) it exhibits any other documents necessary to establish any matter mentioned in paragraph (2)(a) and (d) to (i)` IS A BOOLEAN

