-- Paragraph (2)(b) "either of the following: (i) approved ... or (ii) concluded before the chosen court" and (e) "either of the following"
-- are read as satisfied by either limb, or both (a fork, NOTES.md).
DECLARE `o 37 r 3(2) supporting affidavit` HAS
    `o 37 r 3(2) it states the matters to the best of the information or belief of the deponent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 3(2)(a) it states that the contract is a judicial settlement within the meaning of section 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 3(2)(b)(i) it states that the judicial settlement was approved by a chosen court designated in an exclusive choice of court agreement between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 3(2)(b)(ii) it states that the judicial settlement was concluded before the chosen court in the course of proceedings before that court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 3(2)(c) it states that the judicial settlement, or the part, is enforceable in the same manner and to the same extent as a judgment in the State of origin` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 3(2)(d) it states that the exclusive choice of court agreement was concluded in a civil or commercial matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 3(2)(e)(i) it states that at the date of the application the judicial settlement, or the part, has not been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 3(2)(e)(ii) it states the amount in respect of which, at the date of the application, the judicial settlement, or the part, remains unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 3(2)(f) it states that the judicial settlement does not relate to a matter mentioned in section 9 or 10` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 3(2)(g) it states that there are no circumstances mentioned in section 20(3) in which the Court must refuse to enforce` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 3(2)(h) it states whether there are any circumstances mentioned in section 20(4) in which the Court may refuse to enforce` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 37 r 3(2)(i) it states each reason why the Court should nevertheless enforce the judicial settlement` IS A BOOLEAN

