-- src:5354 | 4. For the purposes of assisting the Court in determining an application mentioned in Rule 2 or 3, the application may be accompanied by a document, issued by a court of the State of origin (or an officer of that court), in the form mentioned in Article 13(3) of the Convention (being a form which is recommended and published by the Hague Conference on Private International Law, and is of the version in force on the date the application is made).
@ref O 37 r 4 (src:5354-5354)
GIVEN `it is an application mentioned in Rule 2 or 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is issued by a court of the State of origin (or an officer of that court)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is in the form mentioned in Article 13(3) of the Convention, of the version in force on the date the application is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 37 r 4 the application may be accompanied by the document` MEANS
    IF `it is an application mentioned in Rule 2 or 3` AND `the document is issued by a court of the State of origin (or an officer of that court)` AND `the document is in the form mentioned in Article 13(3) of the Convention, of the version in force on the date the application is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a "may be accompanied by a document ... in the form mentioned"; the text does not say that no other document may accompany the application

