-- (b) applies "where the Court order and a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement were served on the applicant".
-- The period is 28 days after that service, or "such longer period as the Court may allow".
-- src:5381 | ( b )
-- src:5382 | must, where the Court order and a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement were served on the applicant, be filed within — (i)
-- src:5383 | 28 days after the date on which the Court order, and the copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement (as the case may be), were served on the applicant; or
-- src:5384 | (ii)
-- src:5385 | such longer period as the Court may allow.
@ref O 37 r 7(1)(b) (src:5381-5385)
GIVEN `the Court order and a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement were served on the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application to set aside was filed` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the last day of such longer period as the Court has allowed` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 37 r 7(1)(b) the application to set aside is filed in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Court order and a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement were served on the applicant` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the Court order and a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement were served on the applicant"
        IF `the date the application to set aside was filed` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the last day of such longer period as the Court has allowed`
            WHEN JUST longer THEN
                IF `the date the application to set aside was filed` AT MOST longer
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "28 days after the date on which the Court order ... [was] served on the applicant; or ... such longer period as the Court may allow"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): 28 days passed and the Court allowed no longer period

