-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 8 -- when a Court order takes effect`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The bar, ruling of 2026-11-05 (d): TRUE while an application to set aside may still be filed under Rule 7(1)(b) by a party
-- served under Rule 6, or is pending; FALSE once neither holds.  The text says when the order does NOT take effect, and
-- nothing about when it does, so the twin below answers NOTHING after the bar.
-- src:5393 | 8. A Court order does not take effect while an application to set aside the Court order — ( a )
-- src:5394 | may still be filed under Rule 7(1)( b ) by a party on whom the Court order, and a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement to which the Court order relates, were served under Rule 6; or
@ref O 37 r 8(a) (src:5393-5394)
GIVEN `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which an application to set aside may still be filed by a party on whom the Court order and the copy were served under Rule 6` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 37 r 8(a) an application to set aside may still be filed under Rule 7(1)(b) by a party served under Rule 6` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day on which an application to set aside may still be filed by a party on whom the Court order and the copy were served under Rule 6`
    WHEN JUST last THEN `the date asked about` AT MOST last
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:5393 | 8. A Court order does not take effect while an application to set aside the Court order — ( a )
-- src:5394 | may still be filed under Rule 7(1)( b ) by a party on whom the Court order, and a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement to which the Court order relates, were served under Rule 6; or
-- src:5395 | ( b )
-- src:5396 | is pending.
@ref O 37 r 8 (src:5393-5396)
GIVEN `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which an application to set aside may still be filed by a party on whom the Court order and the copy were served under Rule 6` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `an application to set aside the Court order is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 37 r 8 the Court order does not take effect yet` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an application to set aside the Court order is pending` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 37 r 8(a) an application to set aside may still be filed under Rule 7(1)(b) by a party served under Rule 6` `the date asked about` `the last day on which an application to set aside may still be filed by a party on whom the Court order and the copy were served under Rule 6` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A Court order does not take effect while an application to set aside the Court order (a) may still be filed ...; or (b) is pending"; neither holds

-- src:5393 | 8. A Court order does not take effect while an application to set aside the Court order — ( a )
-- src:5394 | may still be filed under Rule 7(1)( b ) by a party on whom the Court order, and a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement to which the Court order relates, were served under Rule 6; or
-- src:5395 | ( b )
-- src:5396 | is pending.
@ref O 37 r 8 (src:5393-5396)
GIVEN `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which an application to set aside may still be filed by a party on whom the Court order and the copy were served under Rule 6` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `an application to set aside the Court order is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 37 r 8 the Court order takes effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 37 r 8 the Court order does not take effect yet` `the date asked about` `the last day on which an application to set aside may still be filed by a party on whom the Court order and the copy were served under Rule 6` `an application to set aside the Court order is pending`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A Court order does not take effect while"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is over; the rule says only when the order does not take effect

