-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 37 -- the same duties as regulative rules`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The text names no consequence of a late act, so a late act is a BREACH only in the sense that the period has run
-- (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do).  Days are a plain count; the count the Rules require
-- is O 3 r 3 (see the decision functions).

DECLARE `o 37 party under Order 37` IS ONE OF
    `o 37 r 6(2) the applicant`
    `o 37 r 7(2) the applicant to set aside`
    `o 37 r 7(3) the respondent`

DECLARE `o 37 act under Order 37` IS ONE OF
    `o 37 r 6(2)(b) serve the Court order with a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement`
    `o 37 r 6(5) file the affidavit of service`
    `o 37 r 7(1)(b) file the application to set aside`
    `o 37 r 7(2) serve the application and supporting affidavit`
    `o 37 r 7(3) file and serve an affidavit in reply`

-- src:5368 | ( b )
-- src:5369 | within 28 days after the date on which the Court order (relating to the foreign judgment or judicial settlement) is made, serve the Court order, together with a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement, personally on every party to the case or proceedings in which the foreign judgment or judicial settlement was obtained.
@ref O 37 r 6(2)(b) (src:5368-5369)
`o 37 r 6(2)(b) the duty to serve the Court order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 37 r 6(2) the applicant`
    MUST `o 37 r 6(2)(b) serve the Court order with a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement`
    WITHIN (`o 37 r 6(2)(b) the period for serving the Court order`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 37 r 6(2) the applicant` BECAUSE "the Court order was not served within 28 days after it was made"

-- src:5377 | (5) The applicant in paragraph (2) must, within 14 days after the date on which the Court order, and the copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement, are served on a party, file an affidavit of service on that party, of the Court order and the copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement.
@ref O 37 r 6(5) (src:5377-5377)
`o 37 r 6(5) the duty to file the affidavit of service` MEANS
    PARTY `o 37 r 6(2) the applicant`
    MUST `o 37 r 6(5) file the affidavit of service`
    WITHIN (`o 37 r 6(5) the period for filing the affidavit of service`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 37 r 6(2) the applicant` BECAUSE "the affidavit of service was not filed within 14 days after service"

-- src:5381 | ( b )
