@ref O 37 r 7(1)(b) (src:5381-5385)
`o 37 r 7(1)(b) the duty to file the application to set aside` MEANS
    PARTY `o 37 r 7(2) the applicant to set aside`
    MUST `o 37 r 7(1)(b) file the application to set aside`
    WITHIN (`o 37 r 7(1)(b) the period for filing the application to set aside`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 37 r 7(2) the applicant to set aside` BECAUSE "the application to set aside was not filed within 28 days after service"

-- src:5386 | (2) The applicant must, within 14 days after the date on which the application and supporting affidavit are filed, serve the application and supporting affidavit on the following parties (each called in this Rule a respondent): ( a )
-- src:5387 | the party who obtained the Court order;
-- src:5388 | ( b )
-- src:5389 | every other party to the case or proceedings in which the foreign judgment or judicial settlement was obtained.
@ref O 37 r 7(2) (src:5386-5389)
`o 37 r 7(2) the duty to serve the application and supporting affidavit` MEANS
    PARTY `o 37 r 7(2) the applicant to set aside`
    MUST `o 37 r 7(2) serve the application and supporting affidavit`
    WITHIN (`o 37 r 7(2) the period for serving the application and supporting affidavit`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 37 r 7(2) the applicant to set aside` BECAUSE "the application and supporting affidavit were not served within 14 days after they were filed"

-- Paragraph (3) is a MAY.  On main a MAY with no LEST is FULFILLED whether or not the respondent uses it, so no trace can
-- show the window closing; the decision function `o 37 r 7(3) the respondent may file and serve the affidavit in reply` does.
-- src:5390 | (3) Each respondent may, within 21 days after being served with the application and supporting affidavit, file, and serve on the applicant and every other respondent, an affidavit in reply.
@ref O 37 r 7(3) (src:5390-5390)
`o 37 r 7(3) the respondent's permission to file and serve an affidavit in reply` MEANS
    PARTY `o 37 r 7(3) the respondent`
    MAY `o 37 r 7(3) file and serve an affidavit in reply`
    WITHIN (`o 37 r 7(3) the period for the affidavit in reply`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
